# One line ending everywhere. Git for Windows checks CRLF out by default, which
# is not a cosmetic difference here: dprint reports every checkout file as
# "Text differed by line endings" on the Windows CI job, and tests that compare
# file text see the same drift. `text=auto` keeps binary detection; `eol=lf`
# pins the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalise, never diff, never merge.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
# The vendored upstream subtrees under repos/ are 183 MB of 26815 files that no flake, workflow or action reads. Every
# `github:systemfsoftware/effect-endgame-starter-kit` flake input downloads and unpacks this archive on a cold runner.
/repos/ export-ignore
# CONSTITUTION.md is a symlink into repos/; the Actions runner fails on a symlink whose target the archive lacks.
/CONSTITUTION.md export-ignore
